Gunship development build

Enhanced framerate (CUSTOM1) is off by default and requires a 68020 or
later. On a 68000 the option is ignored and native timing is retained.
All framerate enhancements use this master option.

The experimental TIMING_RUNTIME build adds a 3 Hz world clock, responsive
player motion and renderer-only object prediction. It remains in development;
ordinary builds retain native timing. On the supported 0658 version the
runtime build also uses an asynchronous double-buffer swap and a CPU-drawn
3D view. Triple buffering is not used. Polygon drawing clears only used span
rows and avoids a redundant trailing wait; required blitter waits remain.
The CPU view clips/composes its cockpit edges to remove two restore blits,
and unchanged instrument needles are retained separately in each buffer.
Panel changes still repaint overlapping needles. The CPU view and cached art
need 36,010 bytes of free fast RAM; if unavailable they keep native drawing.
These changes share the CUSTOM1 master option.

FS-UAE 68040 play setup

The shared full-MMU a1200-040 preset (25 MHz, 2 MB chip, 8 MB fast) now
works with CUSTOM1=1 and CACHE, retaining asynchronous blits. The original
game reused memory before BltClear finished; Enhanced framerate now waits
for completion in the title, menu and game modules. The previous cycle-exact
NOMMU workaround is no longer needed for that corruption. Validation so far
is in FS-UAE, not on real 68040 hardware.
